> is f equal to g?
  ucas: it(f, g) = f
  ucas: that(f, g) = g
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that differ at 1001000 points, e.g. f=-9.98, g=-10: -9.98 vs -10
> is f different from g?
  sorry: I didn't follow "different from g"
> is x^2 unequal to x^2?
  note: read "unequal" as "equal"
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: that(x) = x^2
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)
> is x^2 unequal to x^2 + 1?
  note: read "unequal" as "equal"
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: that(x) = x^2 + 1
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that differ at 1001 points, e.g. x=-10: 100 vs 101
> is x^2 identical to x^2?
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: that(x) = x^2
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)
